# 18.13 Hypothesis testing and confidence intervals for the slope
## Example 18.3. Coefficient of expansion of metal rods
n = 20 = 20
b = 8.03E-6 = 8.03E-06
beta0 = 1.23E-5 = 1.23E-05
s2 = 1.3E-6 = 1.3E-06
Sxx = 280810.0 = 280810
S_B = Sqrt(s2/Sxx) = 2.15161910259481E-06
t = (b - beta0)/S_B = -1.98455200311731
t_abs = Abs(t) = 1.98455200311731
v = n - 2 = 18
t_crit = MATH.ICDF.STU(0,1,v,0.95) = 1.73406360661752
rejectH0 = t_abs > t_crit = 1
/ reject H0 and conclude statistical evidence supports the claim that coef. is at most beta0
